Tests in this directory were copied from xfstests
(<https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/fs/xfs/xfstests-dev.git>) and have not
yet been converted to sfs traces.  Unless otherwise noted they are from
the tests/generic subdirectory of xfstests.  The actual tests are the
.sh files (shell scripts); the .out files are the expected successful
output under some (usually unspecified) conditions.

Some of these tests may not actually be useful for this lab.
In particular, anything that revolves around a feature of the complete
Unix file I/O API that _isn't_ already mentioned in sfs-api.h (either as
an existing feature or as something we might want to add) can be deleted.
Do think about whether it could be turned into a meaningful test of a
feature SFS does implement, first, though.

Whenever you convert an .sh file to an sfs trace (one or more .lua files
in the parent directory) make sure to delete the original .sh file and
the corresponding .out files so that future lab developers will know
that one has been converted.

xfstests is licensed GPLv2.0.
